# What the image's build never reads (Dockerfile; round 7, audit parity-architecture-02): the owner's data folder, builds, caches, the scratch area and
# the tests
data
release
.scratch
.git
backend/tests
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules
# Settings and passwords that stay on their machine: a filled-in .env.production (the server's secrets), any other .env file (the demo seed's .env.founder),
# and the demo seed's list of passwords. The image takes its settings from the server's environment only
**/.env*
demo/*.local.md
# The web app is the gridlytics-frontend repository's; the image holds the API only, so a copy of it placed here is not sent either
frontend
